      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alden%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Alden sits in the Southeast Quarter of Section 15 and the Northeast Quarter of Section 23, Township 46 N, Range 6 E of the Third Principal Meridian.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alden%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Situated on the West Chicago and Marengo moraines, Alden Township occupies the highest ground in McHenry County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alden%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The glacial moraines form a watershed divide between the Fox and Rock Rivers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alden%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Nippersink Creek, Lawrence Creek, Mokeler Creek, and the North Branch of the Kishwaukee River all drain from the township to the Fox and Rock Rivers.",
